clause: ( A B ) → / A C / = / A B /
just: G.10 • I.Def.15 | circle_radii
say: [sfx:equal] Since A is the center of circle A B, segment A C equals segment A B. <pause>

[screen: ASSERT]
show: *
active: B, ( B A )
equal: / C B /, / A B /
symbolic: ( B A ) → / B C / = / B A /
clause: ( B A ) → / B C / = / B A /
just: G.10 • I.Def.15 | circle_radii
say: [sfx:equal] Since B is the center of circle B A, segment B C also equals segment B A. <pause>

[screen: ASSERT]
show: *
active: A, B, / A B /
equal: / C A /, / C B /
ticks: / C A /, / A B /, / C B /
symbolic: / C A / = / A B /, / B C / = / A B / → / C A / = / B C /
clause: / C A / = / A B /, / B C / = / A B / | → / C A / = / B C /
just: G.16 • I.C.N.1 | equal_transitive
say: [sfx:equal] Things equal to the same thing are equal to one another, so A C, A B, and B C are all equal. <pause>

[screen: ∴ | punchline: true]
show: *
active: < A B C >
equal: / C A /, / A B /, / C B /
symbolic: / C A / = / A B / = / B C / → < A B C >
clause: / C A / = / A B / = / B C / → < A B C >
just: G.13 • I.Def.20 | triangle_sides_def
say: [sfx:qed] Therefore triangle A B C is equilateral, constructed on the given segment A B, <pause> as was required to do.
